 `kscript-backend-v2/docs/local-setup-runbook.md` in that repo.
 
 Rooms recovery and alert handling live with each owning feature; use the supporting-doc table in the [feature index](../features/README.md#related-docs).
+
+## Offline local background workers
+
+`LOCAL_BACKGROUND_WORKERS_DISABLED=true` prevents `App.listen` from starting background workers, Telegram bootstrap and kScript reconcilers in local environments. Staging and production ignore this flag. It defaults off; shutdown remains safe when workers were never started. It does not disable API authentication or replace network egress restrictions.
+
+`MONGO_WAIT_QUEUE_TIMEOUT_MS` configures the Mongo driver connection-pool checkout timeout (default 10000 ms). A cold development database on HDD may need a longer explicit value while boot creates indexes; this does not disable index creation or relax authentication.
